Hello,

I am happy to announce that we will have our traditional Buildroot
Developers Meeting in Brussels right after the FOSDEM conference on
February 3-5, 2020. As usual, Google is sponsoring the event by
providing the meeting location.

More details:

  https://elinux.org/Buildroot:DeveloperDaysFOSDEM2020

This meeting is open to all Buildroot contributors, and allows to
discuss current Buildroot topics, make progress on pending patch
series, reduce the backlog, improve the Buildroot tooling, work on
build issues or new features, and more. It is also a very nice social
moment, with lots of discussions between Buildroot developers on a wide
range of topics.

The event is free, you simply need to register on the Wiki page. We
also have some travel funding available if your travel to the meeting
is not covered by your employer, do not hesitate to contact me
privately if that is the case.

I really encourage regular Buildroot contributors to join this meeting!

Best regards,

